Strategic Rationale
This prioritization strategy follows several key principles:
Foundation First: We prioritize building a solid infrastructure (observability, configuration) before adding advanced features.
User Experience Early: The unified dashboard is prioritized early to make the system immediately more usable for you as a single operator.
Performance Before Features: Critical path optimization comes before new capabilities to ensure the system can handle more complex operations.
Balanced Alpha Generation: Strategy orthogonality and alternative data integration are balanced to ensure both diversification and unique alpha sources.
Risk Management Throughout: Each phase includes improvements to risk management to ensure capital preservation.
Implementation Approach
To implement this efficiently, we'll follow these practices:
Incremental Development: Each component will be built in small, testable increments rather than all at once.
Testing Throughout: Every new component will include unit and integration tests from the beginning.
Documentation as Code: Documentation will be updated alongside code to maintain accuracy.
Configuration-Driven: All new components will be fully configurable without code changes.
Backward Compatibility: During transition, we'll maintain compatibility with existing components.
Key Success Metrics
We'll measure success using these metrics:
System Stability: Zero unexpected shutdowns or failures
Execution Latency: <500μs for order book processing, <1ms for routing decisions
Operational Efficiency: <30 minutes daily for routine operations
Strategy Performance: Reduced correlation between strategies (average <0.3)
Code Quality: >90% test coverage, zero critical bugs
Conclusion
By following this prioritized approach, we'll systematically enhance the Instinct AI system for significant performance improvements while maintaining a manageable development process. The focus on infrastructure, performance, and user experience will ensure the system is both powerful and practical for single-operator usage.